  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Primary request paths (confirmed)",
      "items": [
        "Browser fetches /api/* JSON and the static UI from one FastAPI app on :8099",
        "REST views (plan, person, safeguards, outcomes, decisions) read the engine built once at startup",
        "AI questions pass the rate limiter, then the supervisor, planner, verifier, engine.query() tool, writer and safety agents",
        "safeguards.segment_table(engine) is called by GET /api/safeguards and by the safeguards reporter agent"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Security and trust (confirmed)",
      "items": [
        "No authentication: no route declares a sign-in dependency; only the two AI routes are rate-limited",
        "GEMINI_API_KEY is read from a git-ignored .env and sent only in the x-goog-api-key header",
        "Gemini is used in every environment; Ollama only on a local run (WIQAYA_ENV=local, the default)",
        "The API never returns the hidden _truth block; tested by the QA suite"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Persistence (confirmed)",
      "items": [
        "No database: population, plans and clinician decisions live in Python memory and are lost on restart",
        "The only file read at runtime besides the UI is .env, read once at import"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Assumptions and unknowns",
      "items": [
        "One uvicorn worker is assumed; the rate limit and state are per process, so several workers would not share them",
        "Gemini availability is not probed: status() reports online when a key is set",
        "No deployment config exists in the repo; the diagram shows the local run only",
        "Deployments are assumed to set WIQAYA_ENV=production; without it the app treats itself as a local run"
      ]
    }
  ]
